      "parameters": {
        "color": "#0D0D0D",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 992,
        "content": "## bulk certificates generation with bulkcertify\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow manually starts a bulk certificate generation process using recipient data from Google Sheets. It sends the rows to Bulkcertify, waits and polls the batch status until completion, then retrieves the generated results. After completion it downloads the full ZIP archive and also splits the recipient list to download individual PNG certificates where URLs are available.\n\n### Setup steps\n\nHere is how to get started:\n1. Go to [BulkCertify website](https://bulkcertify.app/) and create a free account.\n2. Navigate to **Developer** to generate your API Key.\n3. In this workflow, replace the Authorization header in the HTTP Request nodes with your free API key (e.g. `Bearer YOUR_KEY`).\n4. Review the [API Docs](https://bulkcertify.app/developer-docs) for more details.\n5. then replace your API key in the nodes\n\nImportant:\n- Configure Google Sheets credentials in n8n and select the spreadsheet/range that contains two column (recipients, their emails).\n- Configure the Bulkcertify HTTP Request nodes with the correct API base URL, authentication headers/API key, batch payload, and batch ID expressions.\n- Verify the request body maps the Google Sheets columns to the fields expected by the Bulkcertify batch generation endpoint.\n- Set binary/download options on the ZIP and PNG download HTTP nodes according to where you want files stored or passed next.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the 15-second polling delay, change which certificate formats are downloaded, or extend the final download nodes to save files to cloud storage, the workflow will email them automatically if you set (\"send_emails\": true)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9b2a6b26-4b9d-495e-b643-2f7068793b75",
